course: dictionary
lesson: 10637
title: Unhelpful and the prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a small group of letters at the start of a word that changes its meaning. The prefix un- often means not, so unhelpful means not helping. «Checking "is that really true?" is called challenging unhelpful thoughts.» Unhelpful thoughts do not help you feel better.
explain: Unhelpful can also mean making a problem or a situation harder. If you feel nervous and a friend says, «Just stop being scared», that comment is unhelpful. It does not help you calm down, and it may make you feel worse.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Vague instructions are unhelpful» makes sense if unhelpful means not helping. If your meaning fits the sentence, you have probably got it right.
fact: Unhelpful means not helping, or making a problem or a situation harder.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, so unkind means not kind and unhelpful means not helpful.
fact: An «unhelpful comment» is a remark that does not help and can make things worse.
fact: Unclear instructions are unhelpful, because they do not tell you what to do.
fact: Helpful is the opposite of unhelpful: helpful gives support, and unhelpful does not.
exercise: «Checking "is that really true?" is called challenging unhelpful thoughts.» What does unhelpful mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Very kind and friendly | Full of colour | *Not helping you feel better
exercise: Mum says, «It is unhelpful to shout when we are trying to fix the problem.» What does she mean? | Shouting makes the room quiet | Shouting is the best way to solve a problem | *Shouting makes the problem harder to fix | Shouting is fun for everyone
exercise: The word unhelpful starts with the prefix un-. What does un- usually mean? | Before | *Not | Again | Very
test: Which word means not helpful? | Helpful | Helpfully | Helper | *Unhelpful
test: A friend says, «Your drawing is rubbish, just give up.» Why is that unhelpful? | It is a question about the drawing | It makes the drawing better | It gives helpful advice | *It makes the problem harder and does not help
exam: Which sentence uses unhelpful correctly? | The unhelpful sunshine made the sky blue | Unhelpful is a kind of fruit | The clear map was unhelpful | *The vague map was unhelpful, because nobody could find the way
